dxp2800-fan is fan control for the UGREEN NASync DXP2800.

It provides itefan, which reads and sets the fan PWM outputs of the
ITE IT8613E Super I/O chip in that machine (and similar boards) by
talking to the chip's environment controller through /dev/io.

fancurve is a small rc(8) service built on itefan. It sets the fan
speed from the hottest CPU core (coretemp(4)) and, optionally, the
hottest disk (smartmontools), and returns the fan to the chip's
automatic mode when stopped. The curve is configured in rc.conf(5).
